{title: O Come to the Altar}
{song_number: 25}
{language: en}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[G]Are you hurting and [C]broken within?
[G]Overwhelmed by the [C]weight of your sin?
[Em]Jesus is [C]calling.
[G]Have you come to the [C]end of yourself?
[G]Do you thirst for a [C]drink from the well?
[Em]Jesus is [C]calling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O come to [Am]the altar; the [Em]Father's arms are [C]open wide. [G]
For[Am]giveness was bought with the [Em]precious blood of [C]Jesus Christ. [G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[G]Leave behind your re[C]grets and mistakes.
[G]Come today; there's [C]no reason to wait.
[Em]Jesus is [C]calling.
[G]Bring your sorrows and [C]trade them for joy.
[G]From the ashes a [C]new life is born.
[Em]Jesus is [C]calling.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O come to [Am]the altar; the [Em]Father's arms are [C]open wide. [G]
For[Am]giveness was bought with the [Em]precious blood of [C]Jesus Christ. [G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
Oh, what a [G]Saviour, isn't He [Em]wonderful?
Sing alle[C]luia, Christ is [G]risen.
Bow down be[Em]fore Him, for He is [C]Lord of all;
sing alle[G]luia, Christ is risen.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
O come to [Am]the altar; the [Em]Father's arms are [C]open wide. [G]
For[Am]giveness was bought with the [Em]precious blood of [C]Jesus Christ. [G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[G]Bear your cross [C]as you wait for the crown;
[G]tell the world [F]of the treasure you've [G]found.
{end_of_verse}
